No - I mean that a player *can* do it, with the current version of the
game, if they're patient and careful enough.  Although thinking about it
more, you don't need to pray at all, so luck management (and avoiding
getting crowned) doesn't get involved at all.

A neutral player with a HoOA (and a large supply of ways to remove
the curse on it), can become either one of the other alignments at will.
Once you've become lawful, go and dip for Excalibur, and once you're
chaotic, sacrifice until you're given Stormbringer (there aren't *that*
many chaotic artifacts).  Then revert to neutral, and either sacrifice
some more until you're given Vorpy, or find another long sword and get
yourself crowned.

